verify-digest-signature-scheme: TPM2_VerifyDigestSignature checks the key scheme, the digest size and the signature scheme

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Library, Part 3 (version 185),
"TPM2_VerifyDigestSignature", "General Description"):

  "The scheme of keyHandle must be a signing scheme that supports signing a
  digest (e.g., TPM_ALG_ECDSA). The size of digest must match the size of the
  hash algorithm of the signing scheme.

  The TPM will verify that the signing scheme (including the hash or XOF
  algorithm) in signature matches the signing scheme of keyHandle
  (TPM_RC_SCHEME)."

Part 3, Table "Signing commands overview": HMAC with TPM2_SignDigest() /
TPM2_VerifyDigestSignature() is "Not supported".

Apart from ML-DSA keys, TPM2_VerifyDigestSignature verifies the signature like
TPM2_VerifySignature, with the scheme and hash algorithm of the signature: a
key without a signing scheme of its own or with TPM_ALG_HMAC is accepted, a
digest of any size is verified, and a signature of another scheme or hash
than the key's (e.g., RSAPSS for an RSASSA key) is verified instead of
rejected. The command now checks, in this order: the key's scheme
(CryptoCommon_SelectSignScheme() with a NULL selector; failure or TPM_ALG_HMAC
is TPM_RC_SCHEME + RC_VerifyDigestSignature_keyHandle), the digest size
(TPM_RC_SIZE + RC_VerifyDigestSignature_digest) and the signature's scheme and
hash algorithm (TPM_RC_SCHEME + RC_VerifyDigestSignature_signature), as in
tpm-rs.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/VerifyDigestSignature.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/VerifyDigestSignature.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/VerifyDigestSignature.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/VerifyDigestSignature.c
@@ -71,6 +71,29 @@ TPM2_VerifyDigestSignature(
         if(in->context.t.size != 0)
             return TPM_RCS_VALUE + RC_VerifyDigestSignature_context;
 
+        // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+        // "The scheme of keyHandle must be a signing scheme that supports signing
+        // a digest (e.g., TPM_ALG_ECDSA). The size of digest must match the size
+        // of the hash algorithm of the signing scheme. The TPM will verify that
+        // the signing scheme (including the hash or XOF algorithm) in signature
+        // matches the signing scheme of keyHandle (TPM_RC_SCHEME)." (Part 3,
+        // TPM2_VerifyDigestSignature)
+        {
+            TPMT_SIG_SCHEME objectScheme;
+            TPMI_ALG_HASH   schemeHashAlg;
+            //
+            objectScheme.scheme = TPM_ALG_NULL;
+            if(!CryptoCommon_SelectSignScheme(signObject, &objectScheme)
+               || objectScheme.scheme == TPM_ALG_HMAC)
+                return TPM_RCS_SCHEME + RC_VerifyDigestSignature_keyHandle;
+            schemeHashAlg = CryptoCommon_GetSignSchemeHashAlg(&objectScheme);
+            if(in->digest.t.size != CryptoCommon_HashGetDigestSize(schemeHashAlg))
+                return TPM_RCS_SIZE + RC_VerifyDigestSignature_digest;
+            if(in->signature.sigAlg != objectScheme.scheme
+               || CryptoCommon_GetSignHashAlg(&in->signature) != schemeHashAlg)
+                return TPM_RCS_SCHEME + RC_VerifyDigestSignature_signature;
+        }
+
         // Validate Signature.  TPM_RC_SCHEME, TPM_RC_HANDLE or TPM_RC_SIGNATURE
         // error may be returned by CryptoCommon_ValidateDigestSignature()
         result = CryptoCommon_ValidateDigestSignature(
